--TEST--
`isOpen` is a `Core\Db\Connection` member and not one a `Core\Db\Transaction` delegates, so the question is asked of the handle that can be closed — `rule:core-classes/db-one-api` and `rule:core-classes/db-transactions`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Db\Connection::isOpen
// A `Core\Db\Transaction` carries every `Queryable` member of the connection it
// runs on, and `close`, `driver`, `serverVersion` and `isOpen` are the four
// that are not `Queryable`'s. `rule:core-classes/db-transactions` is why: a transaction lives for the
// length of one callable and nothing inside it can release the connection, so
// "is this still open" has no answer to give there that is not already `true`.
class Step {
    public static function run(Core\Db\Transaction $tx): bool {
        return $tx->isOpen();
    }
}

// The same question of the handle that owns the connection, which is accepted.
var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");
bool $state = $db->isOpen();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Core\Db\Transaction` has no method named `isOpen`
   --> case.nvs:10:16
